+
+### M1 operational specification
+
+The fixed execution domains are independent: `263.15<=Tleaf_sun,Tleaf_shade
+<=273.15 K`, `263.15<=Tstem<=278.15 K`, and
+`258.15<=Tair,Tcan,Twet<=278.15 K`. Pressure is `80000<=p<=110000 Pa`.
+The 72-hour warm continuation retains the same `(M,H)` state and uses the
+existing liquid constitutive path with every component temperature in
+`273.15..373.15 K`. `PAR=0`, positive leaf area, supplied liquid conducting
+tissue, liquid-accessible `FullSupply` roots, and supplied effective `g0`,
+hydraulic, and `Rd` coefficients are `ASSUMED_FOR_EXECUTION` predicates, not
+observed certification. A missing predicate is `VEG-E-140`; no parameter is
+retuned when a saturation branch crosses `Tf`.
+
+For phase `j in {liq,ice}`, set `a_j=cp_j-cpv`,
+`L_j(T)=Lj0-a_j*(T-Tf)`,
+`e_j=e0*(Tf/T)^(a_j/Rv)*exp(Lj0/(Rv*Tf)-L_j(T)/(Rv*T))`, and
+`de_j/dT=e_j*L_j(T)/(Rv*T^2)`. Then
+`q_j=.622*e_j/(p-.378*e_j)` and
+`dq_j/dT=.622*p*(de_j/dT)/(p-.378*e_j)^2`. Require finite `p` and
+`p-.378e_j>0`. At `Tf`, use `e0` and the liquid-side derivative for the
+internal-liquid branch; the external mixed branch has common `e0` but retains
+its selected one-sided derivative. These are `VEG-E-141` guards. The exact
+Ambaum PDF digest and equations are
+the immutable source register (`Ambaum2020.pdf`, SHA-256
+`53a2f41897205a66ca6db78bd4f48311f4b7f6cda35ccdea300d8d51be196c5e`,
+equation map and source URLs); R156 supplies `Tf,Cw,Ci`, SURFEX supplies `Lf`.
+Their litter kinetics/capacity/saturation do not transfer.
+
+Empty `M=H=0` has `fwet=0` and no wet temperature. Its supersaturation guard
+uses each existing dry leaf temperature with its internal-liquid saturation:
+if `qcan>q_sat_liquid_internal(Tleaf_sun,p)` or
+`qcan>q_sat_liquid_internal(Tleaf_shade,p)`, reject `VEG-E-142`; otherwise set
+wet `E=Q=D=0` when `I=0`. Thus M1 has no implicit dry-surface condensation initiation.
+An empty state becomes nonempty only through an authenticated incident liquid
+`I>0` with supplied `hI`; that branch uses the incident liquid temperature
+diagnosed from `hI=Cw*(T-Tf)`.
+
+For positive `M`, evaluator state selects `alpha` from `(M,H)` as `ice`,
+`mixed`, `liquid`, or `liquid-cap`, with ties selecting mixed at
+`H=-Lf*M` and `H=0`, and cap at `ml=Cliq`. `alpha` is the piecewise physical
+residual evaluated at each Newton state, not a retry path selected after a
+failed solve. Phase boundaries are continuous backward-Euler constitutive
+changes within the existing `dt>=60 s` support; they create no temporal split
+or post-phase update. `D` is algebraically eliminated. Define
+`D=(M0+dt*(I-E)-M1)/dt`; for non-cap alpha use
+`R_M=M1-M0-dt*(I-E)=0`, while cap alpha replaces it by
+`R_cap=min(dt*D,Cliq-ml)=0` in `kg m^-2`. Acceptance requires `D>=0`,
+`ml<=Cliq`, and reconstruction of the mass identity. The enthalpy residual is
+always `R_H=H1-H0-dt*(Q+I*hI-E*hv-D*hl)=0`. This one residual family makes
+drainage/capacity part of the coupled balance and forbids postsolve clipping.
+With positive initial storage and evaporation alone, backward Euler approaches
+but does not manufacture a finite-step empty event; exact empty uses the branch
+above, where `M^(2/3)` is deliberately not differentiated.
+
+The exact cold-dark reduction is block triangular, not a reduced physics
+model. In each occupancy V10 fixes `beta_sun=beta_shade=1`, makes `ci`
+analytic, and makes dry energy/vapor/`Rd` independent of the four hydraulic
+potentials under supplied `FullSupply`. First solve the 19-coordinate energy
+block `(Tleaf_sun,Tleaf_shade,Tstem,M,H)` for each of two occupancies, shared
+`(Tcan,qcan)`, one ground coordinate, and six soil coordinates:
+`2*5+2+1+6=19`. Its residual order is the three retained dry-energy residuals,
+the selected `R_M`/`R_cap`, and `R_H` per occupancy, followed by shared-air,
+ground, and soil residuals. Then solve each unchanged four-potential hydraulic
+continuity block using the accepted `Egas`, and reconstruct the full 27
+coordinate/27 residual system: `19+2*4=27`, with four hydraulic residuals per
+occupancy. Any hydraulic failure rejects the whole candidate and never alters
+`E`, `g0`, or alpha. This replaces the warm 29-coordinate system
+(`2*10+2+1+6`) by its zero-PAR exact factorization; a naive retained dense
+form would be 31 (`29-2 wetT+4 M,H`), so the selected evaluator removes four
+fixed beta coordinates and avoids two cap-multiplier allocations. Per
+occupancy it adds one M/H inversion, two named saturation calls, and the two
+mass/enthalpy residual operands; it adds no history state or plant heat store.
+
+Scale `R_M` by `max(M0,abs(I-E)*dt,1e-9 kg m^-2)` and `R_H` by
+`max(abs(H0),abs(Q+I*hI-E*hv)*dt,1 J m^-2)`; require scaled residual
+`<=1e-8`, raw `R_M<=1e-9 kg m^-2`, raw `R_H<=1e-6 J m^-2`, and independent
+`1e-6 J m^-2` ledger reconstruction. Finite differences use `1e-4 K` for
+temperatures, `1e-8 kg kg^-1` for humidity, `1e-3` in hydraulic-potential
+native units, `1e-8 kg m^-2` for `M`, and `1e-3 J m^-2` for `H`; analytic
+saturation derivatives above are used where saturation enters a Jacobian.
+Domain/identity errors precede nonlinear failure, which precedes closure,
+then receipt publication failure.
+
+Fresh V1 initialization supplies `M,H`, incident phase and `hI`, and every
+domain predicate. The retained `0.018 kg m^-2` fixture is fixed at
+`Tinit=273.15 K`, hence `M=.018` and `H=0`; no warm start supplies or infers
+enthalpy. V1 restart serializes this identity plus `(M,H)` and rejects legacy
+liquid-only state.
